{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_014","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"Copy page as Markdown for LLMs","location_hint":"paragraph 215","char_start":4332,"char_end":4362,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_015","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"Create a non-fungible token (NFT) . This is the only opportunity the minter has to specify any token fields and flags that are immutable. This transaction can be sent by the NFT&#x27;s issuer or by an authorized minter .","location_hint":"paragraph 227","char_start":4630,"char_end":4850,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_016","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"If successful, the transaction adds an NFToken object to one of the minter&#x27;s NFTokenPage ledger entries .","location_hint":"paragraph 228","char_start":4852,"char_end":4962,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_017","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"Requires the NonFungibleTokensV1_1 amendment . Loading...","location_hint":"paragraph 229","char_start":4964,"char_end":5021,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_018","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"{\n\"TransactionType\" : \"NFTokenMint\" ,\n\"Account\" : \"rvYAfWj5gh67oV6fW32ZzP3Aw4Eubs59B\" ,\n\"TransferFee\" : 314 ,\n\"NFTokenTaxon\" : 0 ,\n\"Flags\" : 8 ,\n\"Fee\" : \"10\" ,\n\"URI\" : \"697066733A2F2F62616679626569676479727A74357366703775646D37687537367568377932366E6634646675796C71616266336F636C67747179353566627A6469\" ,\n\"Memos\" : [\n{\n\"Memo\" : {\n\"MemoType\" :\n\"687474703A2F2F6578616D706C652E636F6D2F6D656D6F2F67656E65726963\" ,\n\"MemoData\" : \"72656E74\"\n}\n}\n]\n}","location_hint":"paragraph 231","char_start":5053,"char_end":5494,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_019","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"In addition to the common fields , NFTokenMint transactions use the following fields:","location_hint":"paragraph 234","char_start":5543,"char_end":5628,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_020","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"Field JSON Type Internal Type Required? Description","location_hint":"paragraph 235","char_start":5632,"char_end":5683,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_021","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"NFTokenTaxon Number UInt32 Yes An arbitrary taxon , or shared identifier, for a series or collection of related NFTs. To mint a series of NFTs, give them all the same taxon.","location_hint":"paragraph 236","char_start":5687,"char_end":5860,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_022","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"Issuer String - Address AccountID No The issuer of the token, if the sender of the account is issuing it on behalf of another account. This field must be omitted if the account sending the transaction is the issuer of the NFToken . If provided, the issuer&#x27;s AccountRoot object must have the NFTokenMinter field set to the sender of this transaction (this transaction&#x27;s Account field).","location_hint":"paragraph 237","char_start":5862,"char_end":6256,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_023","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"TransferFee Number UInt16 No The value specifies the fee charged by the issuer for secondary sales of the NFToken , if such sales are allowed. Valid values for this field are between 0 and 50000 inclusive, allowing transfer rates of between 0.00% and 50.00% in increments of 0.001. If this field is provided, the transaction MUST have the tfTransferable flag enabled.","location_hint":"paragraph 238","char_start":6258,"char_end":6625,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_024","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"URI String - Hexadecimal Blob No Up to 256 bytes of arbitrary data. In JSON, this should be encoded as a string of hexadecimal. You can use the xrpl.convertStringToHex utility to convert a URI to its hexadecimal equivalent. This is intended to be a URI that points to the data or metadata associated with the NFT. The contents could decode to an HTTP or HTTPS URL, an IPFS URI, a magnet link, immediate data encoded as an RFC 2379 \"data\" URL , or even an issuer-specific encoding. The URI is NOT checked for validity.","location_hint":"paragraph 239","char_start":6627,"char_end":7144,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_025","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"Amount Currency Amount Amount No Indicates the amount expected or offered for the corresponding NFToken . The amount must be non-zero, except where the asset is XRP; then, it is legal to specify an amount of zero, which means that the current owner of the token is giving it away, gratis, either to anyone at all, or to the account identified by the Destination field.","location_hint":"paragraph 240","char_start":7146,"char_end":7514,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_026","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"Expiration Number UInt32 No Time after which the offer is no longer active, in seconds since the Ripple Epoch . Results in an error if the Amount field is not specified.","location_hint":"paragraph 241","char_start":7516,"char_end":7685,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_027","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"Destination String - Address AccountID No If present, indicates that this offer may only be accepted by the specified account. Attempts by other accounts to accept this offer MUST fail. Results in an error if the Amount field is not specified.","location_hint":"paragraph 242","char_start":7687,"char_end":7930,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_028","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"Transactions of the NFTokenMint type support additional values in the Flags field , as follows:","location_hint":"paragraph 244","char_start":7953,"char_end":8048,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_029","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"Flag Name Hex Value Decimal Value Description","location_hint":"paragraph 245","char_start":8052,"char_end":8097,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_030","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"tfBurnable 0x00000001 1 Allow the issuer (or an entity authorized by the issuer) to destroy the minted NFToken . (The NFToken &#x27;s owner can always do so.)","location_hint":"paragraph 246","char_start":8101,"char_end":8259,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_031","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"tfOnlyXRP 0x00000002 2 The minted NFToken can only be bought or sold for XRP. This can be desirable if the token has a transfer fee and the issuer does not want to receive fees in non-XRP currencies.","location_hint":"paragraph 247","char_start":8261,"char_end":8460,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_032","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"tfTrustLine 0x00000004 4 DEPRECATED Automatically create trust lines from the issuer to hold transfer fees received from transferring the minted NFToken . The fixRemoveNFTokenAutoTrustLine amendment makes it invalid to set this flag.","location_hint":"paragraph 248","char_start":8462,"char_end":8695,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_033","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"tfTransferable 0x00000008 8 The minted NFToken can be transferred to others. If this flag is not enabled, the token can still be transferred from or to the issuer, but a transfer to the issuer must be made based on a buy offer from the issuer and not a sell offer from the NFT holder.","location_hint":"paragraph 249","char_start":8697,"char_end":8981,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_034","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"tfMutable 0x00000010 16 The URI field of the minted NFToken can be updated using the NFTokenModify transaction.","location_hint":"paragraph 250","char_start":8983,"char_end":9094,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_035","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"Embedding additional information","location_hint":"paragraph 251","char_start":9098,"char_end":9130,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_036","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"If you need to specify additional information during minting (for example, details identifying a property by referencing a particular plat , a vehicle by specifying a VIN , or other object-specific descriptions) you can use a transaction memo . Memos are a part of the signed transaction and are available from historical archives, but are not stored in the ledger&#x27;s state data.","location_hint":"paragraph 252","char_start":9132,"char_end":9515,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_037","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"Issuing on behalf of another account","location_hint":"paragraph 253","char_start":9517,"char_end":9553,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_038","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"If you want to issue an NFT for another account there are two things you must do. Given that Account A is your account and Account B is the account for which you want to mint a NFToken:","location_hint":"paragraph 254","char_start":9555,"char_end":9740,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_039","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"Set the NFTokenMinter account setting on Account B to be Account A . (This says that Account B trusts Account A to create NFTs on their behalf.)","location_hint":"paragraph 255","char_start":9744,"char_end":9888,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_040","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"When you mint the NFToken, set the Issuer field to Account B.","location_hint":"paragraph 256","char_start":9890,"char_end":9951,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_041","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"Example of NFTokenMint with an issuer","location_hint":"paragraph 257","char_start":9955,"char_end":9992,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_042","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"{\n\"TransactionType\" : \"NFTokenMint\" ,\n\"Account\" : \"rvYAfWj5gh67oV6fW32ZzP3Aw4Eubs59B\" ,\n\"Issuer\" : \"rNCFjv8Ek5oDrNiMJ3pw6eLLFtMjZLJnf2\" ,\n\"TransferFee\" : 25000 ,\n\"NFTokenTaxon\" : 0 ,\n\"Flags\" : 8 ,\n\"Fee\" : \"10\" ,\n\"URI\" : \"697066733A2F2F62616679626569676479727A74357366703775646D37687537367568377932366E6634646675796C71616266336F636C67747179353566627A6469\" ,\n\"Memos\" : [\n{\n\"Memo\" : {\n\"MemoType\" :\n\"687474703A2F2F6578616D706C652E636F6D2F6D656D6F2F67656E65726963\" ,\n\"MemoData\" : \"72656E74\"\n}\n}\n]\n}","location_hint":"paragraph 258","char_start":9998,"char_end":10491,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_043","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"This transaction assumes that the issuer, rNCFjv8Ek5oDrNiMJ3pw6eLLFtMjZLJnf2 , has set the NFTokenMinter field in its AccountRoot to rvYAfWj5gh67oV6fW32ZzP3Aw4Eubs59B , thereby authorizing that account to mint tokens on its behalf.","location_hint":"paragraph 259","char_start":10493,"char_end":10724,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_044","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"Besides errors that can occur for all transactions, NFTokenMint transactions can result in the following transaction result codes :","location_hint":"paragraph 261","char_start":10739,"char_end":10870,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_045","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"temDISABLED The NonFungibleTokensV1 amendment is not enabled.","location_hint":"paragraph 263","char_start":10900,"char_end":10961,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_046","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"temBAD_NFTOKEN_TRANSFER_FEE The TransferFee is not within the acceptable range.","location_hint":"paragraph 264","char_start":10963,"char_end":11042,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_047","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"temINVALID_FLAG The Flags value has bits enabled that are not allowed or valid flags. If the fixRemoveNFTokenAutoTrustLine amendment is enabled, the tfTrustLine flag causes this error.","location_hint":"paragraph 265","char_start":11044,"char_end":11228,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_048","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"temMALFORMED The transaction was not validly specified. For example, the URI field is longer than 256 bytes.","location_hint":"paragraph 266","char_start":11230,"char_end":11338,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
{"excerpt_id":"ex_517d67dc1224_049","source_id":"src_517d67dc1224","source_hash":"1e53936cf0c431419c094b9712f6a770bf87fc44d05e019bdafb4f6460b17c0e","text":"tecNO_ISSUER The Issuer refers to an account that does not exist in the ledger.","location_hint":"paragraph 267","char_start":11340,"char_end":11419,"origin":"raw_text","created_at":"2026-05-09T19:32:46.126Z"}
